# Line endings.
#
# This repository is authored on Windows and its CI runs on ubuntu-latest.
# A shell script committed with CRLF fails on Linux with the error
#
#     /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# or, more confusingly, `$'\r': command not found` on a line that looks
# perfectly correct in the editor. It is the single most common first-CI
# failure for a Windows-authored repository, it costs an afternoon, and it is
# prevented by four lines.

* text=auto

# Files that MUST be LF regardless of the platform they were written on,
# because something other than a human reads them.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.sql      text eol=lf

# .st files are IEC 61131-3 Structured Text, loaded by the OpenPLC runtime
# inside a Linux container. Same argument.
*.st       text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.xlsx     binary
*.png      binary
*.pdf      binary
